ean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival"],"id":"long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.24 (Denominators of finite Mersenne sums)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.24, p. 51, label thm:mersenne-channel-survival","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $t\\ge1$ and $h\\ge1$ be integers, and let $r\\ge1$ be squarefree with every prime factor at most $t$. Let $P$ be a set of prime divisors of $r$ such that $t<2p$ for each $p\\in P$, and put $C=\\prod_{p\\in P}(2^p-1)$. Then\n$$\n\\frac{C}{\\gcd(C,h)}\\ \\bigm|\\ \\operatorname{den}\\bigl(hB(r)\\bigr).\n$$\nIn particular, $C$ divides this reduced denominator when $\\gcd(C,h)=1$. The factors in $C$ are pairwise coprime, since $\\gcd(2^p-1,2^q-1)=2^{\\gcd(p,q)}-1=1$ for distinct primes. The assertion concerns this finite signed sum; it does not replace the approximation hypotheses in Theorem 6.14.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.channelProduct_coprime_mobiusNumerator_of_one_le%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-mersenne-channel-survival%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.channelProduct_coprime_mobiusNumerator_of_one_le%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d